    <fr:title text="Rapidly Exploring Random Trees">Rapidly Exploring Random Trees</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter><html:p>Rapidly exploring random trees (RRT) is a very simple, elegant and widely used algorithm for motion planning. The algorithm proceeds as follows:</html:p>
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);">Algorithm.</html:span> 
  For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[k = 1]]></fr:tex> to <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K]]></fr:tex> do
 <html:ol><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x_{rand} \gets  \mathsf {RANDOM\_STATE}()]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x_{near} \gets  \mathsf {NEAREST\_NEIGHBOR}(x_{rand}, \mathcal {T})]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[u \gets  \mathsf {SELECT\_INPUT}(x_{near})]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x_{new} \gets  \mathsf {NEW\_STATE}(x_{near}, u, \Delta  t)]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {T}.add\_vertex(x_{new})]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {T}.add\_edge((x_{near}, u, x_{new}))]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ol>
 return <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {T}]]></fr:tex>
</html:div>


 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(219, 216, 215);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);">Remark.</html:span> 
Given some dynamics model <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dot {x} = f(x, u)]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {NEW\_STATE}]]></fr:tex> is some approximate integration, such as Euler integration i.e.
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[x_{new} = x_{near} + f(x_{near}, u) \Delta  t]]></fr:tex>
Preferable to use higher-order method like Runge-Kutta.
</html:div>

 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(219, 216, 215);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);">Remark.</html:span> 
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {SELECT\_INPUT}]]></fr:tex> is determined by whether the system is holonomic or non-holomonic. If the agent is holonomic, then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[u]]></fr:tex> will just be the control corresponding to the difference in the two states.
</html:div>
</fr:mainmatter>
